License compliance statements
-----------------------------

1. These copies are NOT modified. The MANIFEST.sha256 in this directory
   pins the SHA-256 of every file; a CI/unit test reconciles the manifest
   against the tree. Any future upstream update must be a fresh verbatim
   copy with a new CHANGELOG.md entry — never an in-place edit.

2. The 81-wavelength spectral arrays carried inside the profiles
   (log_sensitivity, channel_density, midscale_neutral_density and the
   spectral shape of base_density) ARE consumed as a per-wavelength
   material chain: since the M8 spectral film core, Lightamer's film
   simulation integrates the negative's spectral sensitivity and the
   paper's spectral response wavelength by wavelength through the
   material chain (the DIR coupler stage's structure is in place and
   ships neutral — the profile set carries no coupler measurement
   data). The SCENE enters that chain as a metameric reconstruction:
   the consumer-facing capability is full per-wavelength
   material-chain simulation with chromaticity-domain spectral
   upsampling upstream of the material chain ("spectrally
   reconstructed material simulation, per wavelength — not scene
   spectral replay": the scene's spectrum is reconstructed
   metamerically, never replayed). The density-domain consumer face
   remains for the frozen legacy arm: data.log_exposure +
   data.density_curves (256x3), plus base_density sampled at three
   registered wavelengths (650/550/450 nm, nearest neighbour) as an
   RGB constant, and data.wavelengths serving both that sampling and
   the 81-point chain's axis. This consumption statement is disclosed
   here per the license's modifications-transparency spirit; the FILES
   themselves remain untouched.

3. Share-alike scope: the CC BY-SA 4.0 obligations attach to these
   profile assets and their direct derivatives (bake products of this
   data), not to the Lightamer source code that reads them. Derived
   bake assets, if ever distributed with the app, must carry the same
   license and attribution; runtime-generated caches that are not
   distributed leave the obligation on these source files.

4. Isolation: this directory is physically separate from the MIT-licensed
   LUT set (Resources/LUTs/) — no bytes are shared between the two asset
   families.
